   "source": [
    "### Domanda 02\n",
    "\n",
    "**Caricare il dataset**, eliminare eventuali attributi inutili (motivare la scelta), eliminare eventuali istanze con valori nulli, dividere il dataset in train (75%) e test (25%), preservando le proporzioni delle classi del target."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "EumQLd-Fsv6a"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df.drop(\"id\", axis=1, inplace=True)\n",
    "df.dropna(inplace=True)\n",
    "df.drop_duplicates(inplace=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "tIYQiMG4wxA4"
   },
   "source": [
    "> Rimosso l'attributo `id` in quanto può influenzare negativamente le predizioni dei modelli, andando a trovare relazioni tra predizione e questo attributo non non esistono."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "3Jl-yFdAwiPh"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X, y = df.drop(\"HiringDecision\", axis=1), df[\"HiringDecision\"]\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=1/4, random_state=0, stratify=y)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "UWl_YtSBjgw3"
   },
   "source": [
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "A6knmUxzswRT"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Domanda 03\n",
    "\n",
    "Valutare le performance sia sul dataset train sia sul dataset test del modello **SGDClassifier**, tenendo in considerazione F1-score e la confusion matrix."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "3DgEDagxswRV"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "columns = df.drop([\"HiringDecision\", \"Gender\"], axis=1).columns\n",
    "scaler.fit(X_train[columns])\n",
    "X_train[columns] = scaler.transform(X_train[columns])\n",
    "X_test[columns] = scaler.transform(X_test[columns])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "executionInfo": {
     "elapsed": 31,
     "status": "ok",
     "timestamp": 1767286386463,
     "user": {
      "displayName": "LUIGI MALAGUTI",
      "userId": "16283703726180943708"
     },
     "user_tz": -60
    },
    "id": "H604eDt13-VP",
    "outputId": "14399427-ff10-481b-ba7f-4017dc92dbda"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Train\n",
      "  Accuracy: 0.8453333333333334\n",
      "  F1: 0.7379518072289156\n",
      "[[706  70]\n",
      " [104 245]]\n",
      "------------------------------\n",
      "Test\n",
      "  Accuracy: 0.8426666666666667\n",
      "  F1: 0.7467811158798283\n",
      "[[229  30]\n",
      " [ 29  87]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "sgd = SGDClassifier(random_state=0)\n",
    "sgd.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "y_pred_train = sgd.predict(X_train)\n",
    "y_pred_test = sgd.predict(X_test)\n",
    "print(\"Train\")\n",
    "print(\"  Accuracy:\", accuracy_score(y_train, y_pred_train))\n",
    "print(\"  F1:\", f1_score(y_train, y_pred_train))\n",
    "print(confusion_matrix(y_train, y_pred_train))\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 30)\n",
    "print(\"Test\")\n",
    "print(\"  Accuracy:\", accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred_test))\n",
    "print(\"  F1:\", f1_score(y_test, y_pred_test))\n",
    "print(confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred_test))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "GH5wnR4J8xJM"
   },
   "source": [
    "> Dalle metriche possiamo notare come il modello `SGD` abbia una buona accuratezza, quasi 85%, mentre la metrica di F1 è più bassa, quasi 75% sul dataset di test, mentre quasi 74% sul dataset di train."
   ]
